---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---

<section class="wrap sec--how how">
  <div>
    <h2 class="h2 display how__title">Hear the one that bleats.</h2>

    <div class="step">
      <h3 class="display">The dog on the ridge</h3>
      <p>
        A small Go binary on your Herdr host waits on Herdr's{' '}
        <span class="mono">agent.wait</span> for every agent in every session. When one turns
        blocked or done, it barks: one outbound push through your own Firebase project.
        Nothing comes in.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <h3 class="display">The bell reaches you</h3>
      <p>
        The notification opens on that agent. Read what it is asking. Approve, or type a
        reply, from wherever you are sitting. A stale tap does nothing, because the approval
        is keyed to the state it was shown for.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <h3 class="display">Walk down if you must</h3>
      <p>
        For anything a shout will not fix, attach gives you the real terminal on the phone.
        xterm.dart, not a web view. Esc, sticky Ctrl, Tab, arrows.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="note">
      Interactive traffic runs over your tailnet with a per-device token, so one lost phone
      can be turned away without moving the fence.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="how__aside">
    <div class="bezel bezel--phone">
      <picture>
        <source type="image/webp" srcset={`${base}screens/chat-device.webp`} />
        <img
          src={`${base}screens/chat-device.jpg`}
          width="760"
          height="1629"
          loading="lazy"
          alt="An agent's chat on the phone, asking a question with approve and reply below it"
        />
      </picture>
    </div>
    <p class="caption">The bell, answered. One tap from the phone, and the agent is back to work.</p>
  </div>
</section>
